{"items":[{"index":17,"prompt":"Prepare a technical diagram for maintenance trainees that explains how a hydraulic stamping press carries force through its frame. Show the machine in a straight-on front view, large enough that the structure and moving parts are easy to distinguish. Use a colored-pencil texture and a vivid palette, while keeping component colors consistent enough to support the explanation.

Make the upper crossbeam a clearly readable truss: divide the span between the two uprights into four equal rectangular bays, and split each bay with one diagonal, alternating the diagonal direction from bay to bay. This should leave exactly eight visible triangular openings. Keep the brace ends joined cleanly at the truss nodes, and leave the openings unobstructed. Beneath the beam, center a hydraulic cylinder and its descending ram over a broad press platen; show the platen above a sturdy worktable. Include a wide base joining the uprights so the load path can be followed down through the frame.

Use a few purposeful details—a pair of hoses, a control box, and simple guarding—to identify the machine without competing with the truss. Distinguish the ram and platen from the stationary frame by color and clear overlap, but do not cover structural joints. Favor an immediate visual hierarchy: first the press assembly, then its triangular bracing, then the supporting details. Keep the drawing diagrammatic rather than photorealistic, and omit decorative lettering or unrelated workshop scenery.","skills":["composition","relative_geometry","layering"]}]}
